Theorem RL-27: selective ownership-event ordering at calls

  Preconditions:
    - The callee parameter contract is known.

  Soundness property:
    Pending events for v are ordered before the call iff the callee parameter is
    Owned and non-Dead, or Borrowed with may_share. Borrowed pure calls remain
    transparent. "Flush" is only a historical worklist implementation term.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate Owned/non-Dead, Owned/Dead, Borrowed/may_share, Borrowed/pure.
    Coverage gate: 4 cases; Borrowed/pure must not force ordering.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl27_selective_event_ordering)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-27 orders pending ownership events only at call boundaries whose contracts may observe or change ownership state
